  ('75c9c96e-19e6-50ad-b4d7-b92c35f1e817', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Correct binary search errors', 'The following pseudocode is intended to perform a binary search of an ascending sorted array `Item[1:N]`, but it contains errors.

```text
Low ← 1
High ← N
Found ← FALSE

WHILE Low < High AND Found = FALSE
    Middle ← (Low + High) / 2
    IF Item[Middle] = Wanted THEN
        Found ← TRUE
    ELSE
        IF Item[Middle] < Wanted THEN
            High ← Middle - 1
        ELSE
            Low ← Middle + 1
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
ENDWHILE
```

Identify **four** errors and give the correction for each.', 'code_analysis', 4, 'hard', 'analyse', 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', '7724b4d3-9ed5-5292-80da-21e2922c99ae', '{"language":"pseudocode","starter_code":""}'::jsonb, 'original', null, true, 'published', null, null, 0),
  ('9ceaadf8-ab50-5e71-8999-004279272d63', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Write insertion sort', 'Write Cambridge-style pseudocode for an insertion sort that sorts `Name[1:N]` into ascending alphabetic order.', 'pseudocode', 6, 'hard', 'write', 'AI', 11, '90094a74-5e7b-589b-af06-e75a04fd67d7', '7724b4d3-9ed5-5292-80da-21e2922c99ae', '{"language":"pseudocode","starter_code":""}'::jsonb, 'original', null, true, 'published', null, null, 0),
  ('10bcb707-97ec-5702-89a1-75ee74f9fdca', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Trace binary search', 'The array `Number[1:8]` is sorted into ascending order.

| Index | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Number | 3 | 8 | 12 | 19 | 27 | 31 | 45 | 52 |

Trace a binary search for `Wanted ← 27` using this algorithm.

```text
Low ← 1
High ← 8
Found ← FALSE

WHILE Low <= High AND Found = FALSE
    Middle ← (Low + High) DIV 2
    IF Number[Middle] = Wanted THEN
        Found ← TRUE
    ELSE
        IF Number[Middle] < Wanted THEN
            Low ← Middle + 1
        ELSE
            High ← Middle - 1
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
    OUTPUT Low, High, Middle, Number[Middle], Found
ENDWHILE
```

