  ('438bf9b6-3f46-52df-9153-280932fe7e59', 'ea65b685-d0c0-5aa8-bb8d-d6bb01f68d36', 'Toy store data flow diagram', 'A toy store works by following operations:

All data about sold toys (**ToyID, Price, Toy Description**) are stored in the database, **Toy Database**.

• Each toy has a **barcode**.
• A shop assistant scans each chosen toy with a barcode scanner.
• A process, **Generate Bill**, outputs a **Bill** which is presented to the client.
• **Toy Description** and **Price** for each product sold are printed in the bill.', 'structured', 7, 'exam', null, 'AI', 11, 'b670c685-56c9-5476-89b6-b0c02cd8dec7', 'ef6ad158-e13f-5d40-b84a-4d0072e4fdb7', '{}'::jsonb, 'past_paper', 'NIS 2023 Paper 2 Q5', false, 'published', null, null, 0),
