Inserts the stored current score into `Score[Position]` after shifting (1)', '[{"criterion":"Gives a relevant reason for choosing insertion sort.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Uses an outer loop from item 2 to item N.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Stores the current score before shifting.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Initialises a position variable correctly.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Checks the lower bound in the inner loop.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Uses the correct ascending comparison with the previous score.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Shifts larger values right and decrements the position.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Inserts the stored score at the correct position.","marks":1}]'::jsonb, '// Insertion sort is suitable because the list is nearly sorted, so few shifts may be needed.
