Correctly updates `High ← Middle - 1` when the middle code is greater than the wanted code, and outputs either `Stock[Middle]` if found or `"Not found"` otherwise (1)', '[{"criterion":"Initialises search boundaries and found state.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Uses a valid binary search loop condition.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Calculates the middle position using `DIV`.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Correctly detects a matching product code.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Correctly updates the lower boundary when the middle value is too small.","marks":1},{"criterion":"Correctly updates the upper boundary and produces the required final output.","marks":1}]'::jsonb, 'Low ← 1
High ← N
Found ← FALSE

WHILE Low <= High AND Found = FALSE
    Middle ← (Low + High) DIV 2
    IF ProductCode[Middle] = WantedCode THEN
        Found ← TRUE
    ELSE
        IF ProductCode[Middle] < WantedCode THEN
            Low ← Middle + 1
        ELSE
            High ← Middle - 1
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
ENDWHILE

IF Found = TRUE THEN
    OUTPUT Stock[Middle]
ELSE
    OUTPUT "Not found"
ENDIF', '{}'::jsonb, 'Accept storing `FoundPosition ← Middle` on a match and using it after the loop. The final mark requires both correct upper-bound handling and output logic; if one is missing, consider awarding this mark only if the other five marks are fully correct and the omission is minor.', 'The product codes are sorted, so binary search can repeatedly halve the remaining possible positions. The index found in `ProductCode` is also used to access the corresponding value in `Stock`.'),
